{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_b3949f4d07900864\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_b3949f4d07900864/topic_2\", \"topic_label\": \"QA inconsistency on tie judgments\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_cb06b7a6847122af7e6b8e4b\", \"member_bbcf413973c3114c816f502a\", \"member_42af0c53b9dee102697caa09\", \"member_0886e8fe7e7d998c1077ff10\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that QA marked their tie wrong again.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports QA reversing ties even when both outputs fail the same criteria, citing RP-0625.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports in one thread that a tie score passed last week but was flagged on near-identical tasks today, and reports in a later thread that QA marked their tie wrong again on RP-9595.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the RP-9595 thread reports that a QA reviewer accepted a tie yesterday, while a similar pair was marked wrong today.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the reasons in two QA comments use different tie thresholds.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors each say that neither response in the pair discussed in their respective threads has a meaningful quality advantage and that a tie is justified; one also suggests comparing two disputed tasks rather than rewriting policy.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in the RP-0625 thread whether the two pairs really have equivalent strengths and weaknesses.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900725.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900725.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in the RP-9595 thread to compare the written QA rationales against the same rubric criterion.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead acknowledges inconsistent QA feedback in the RP-9595 thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the RP-9595 thread, the team lead asks for both rationales so the judgments can be compared before changing the tie threshold; this instruction is limited to that thread. Verbatim quote: \\\"Please share both rationales so we can calibrate before changing the tie threshold.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current project FAQ directs sharing disputed pairs, relevant prompt requirements and both rationales for comparison, checking whether cases are actually comparable, and not generalizing an answer to one pair without matching its scope.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current project instructions say to choose a tie when neither response has a meaningful quality advantage, reject cosmetic phrasing alone as a reason for preference, and explain the user-facing benefit when selecting on a small difference.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:176ce67d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 16 approval record records the team lead's approval of an announcement and an eight-pair comparison exercise for batch 14, using the existing criterion rather than creating a new numerical threshold; the approval did not record completion and is not a standing rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c14\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 20 batch-14 follow-up records a completed comparison exercise and improved agreement on the same sampled pairs, with one pair still showing disagreement afterward; it is a prior outcome, not a standing rule or evidence of a current-batch resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c15\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The RP-9595 messages provided end with the team lead's request for both rationales and do not include those requested materials.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c16\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The two pair-level replies justify ties for their respective discussed pairs but do not establish why QA judgments differed or show that those reported differences were resolved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors and a tutor report ties being rejected, reversed or flagged across four threads, including RP-0625 and RP-9595.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"In the RP-9595 thread, the team lead acknowledged inconsistent feedback and requested both rationales for comparison before changing the tie threshold.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"On RP-0625, a tutor reports reversals even when both outputs fail the same criteria; a different tutor reports that two QA comments use different tie thresholds.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that a tie score passed last week but was flagged on near-identical tasks today; a tutor in the RP-9595 thread reports an accepted tie followed by rejection of a similar pair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors each say a tie is justified for the pair in their respective threads, without resolving the reported differences between QA judgments.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the RP-0625 pairs have equivalent strengths and weaknesses, and asks in the RP-9595 thread to compare the written rationales against the same rubric criterion.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900725.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900725.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The RP-9595 messages end with the team lead's request; the requested rationales are not included in that thread's evidence.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Earlier batch-14 records show an approved comparison exercise and improved agreement in its reviewed sample, with one sampled pair still showing disagreement afterward; those records are history, not current handling for this batch.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a QA comparison review of the disputed ties, using the pairs, prompt requirements and written rationales required by the FAQ. Draft to copy: Please prepare the disputed tie cases for a QA comparison review:\\n- Two QA tutors report ties marked wrong, including RP-9595; one also reports flags on near-identical tasks after a tie score passed last week.\\n- A tutor reports reversals when both outputs fail the same criteria on RP-0625; a different tutor reports two QA comments using different tie thresholds.\\n- A tutor in the RP-9595 thread reports an accepted tie followed by rejection of a similar pair.\\nPlease provide the disputed pairs, relevant prompt requirements and both written QA rationales. We will check whether the cases are comparable and apply the existing meaningful-quality-advantage criterion. The RP-9595 comparison will precede any change to its tie threshold, as requested in that thread. Scope: Hold the comparison once the case materials are available, and limit conclusions to pairs with matching scope.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:176ce67d\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c15\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c16\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The FAQ calls for comparing disputed pairs and both rationales, rather than assuming similar cases are equivalent. A focused QA review follows that handling without presuming a new tie threshold.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939653.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900676.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:176ce67d\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939697.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900725.000226\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Comparable tie-judgment disputes are reported by distinct authors across four threads, while pair-level replies and a pending request for rationales have not resolved the reported QA differences.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790866003.000036\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790900625.000037\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926534.000040\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939595.000035\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790866050.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790926584.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENE