": \"1790939595.000035\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:14:57.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U019\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can we compare the written QA rationales against the same rubric criterion?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790939731.000339\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_0886e8fe7e7d998c1077ff10\", \"thread_id\": \"1790939595.000035\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T11:15:31.000339Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U019\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"I see inconsistent QA feedback. Please share both rationales so we can calibrate before changing the tie threshold.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-16T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_14): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nPreference batch 14 calibration: choose a tie when neither answer offers a meaningful quality advantage. If choosing A or B, identify the user-facing benefit rather than saying only that it sounds nicer. Keep material factual or instruction-following defects separate. Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review. This message clarifies the existing criterion; it does not create a new numerical threshold.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Ties and preferences\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Ties and preferences\\n\\n### Q: How much improvement is needed to avoid a tie?\\nThe difference must offer a meaningful benefit to the user. Cosmetic phrasing alone usually does not. Explain that benefit; otherwise a tie can be appropriate.\\n\\n### Q: QA is reversing ties on similar pairs. What should I do?\\nShare the pairs, relevant prompt constraints and both rationales for calibration. Check whether the cases are actually comparable. An answer to one pair should not be generalized without matching its scope.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration follow-up — improvement in the reviewed sample\", \"sections\": [\"Review receipt\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"follow_up\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"reported\", \"decision_status\": \"reported\", \"execution_status\": \"calib